# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession gathering build` from data/forever and tools/lib/professions/gathering. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/fishing
title Fishing 1-300
category Professions
coords era
levels 5-60
zone Ironforge

# Fishing 1-300 for both factions. Every catch can raise the skill wherever you
# fish; low skill only makes fish get away in harder waters, so each band sends
# you to water near where you level: the shore beside your starting area's
# fishing trainer, then fishing-pool clusters from objects.json. Expert Fishing
# is a book sold by Old Man Heming in Booty Bay; Artisan Fishing is Nat Pagle's
# quest in Dustwallow Marsh (four rare fish). About 1,300 catches in all.
#
# Spawns come from the reference data: the Era baseline (pfQuest) plus the
# node spawns Forever's beta sniffs add (Zephras Isle, the starting-area Poor
# Copper Veins and herbs: the Forever TrinityCore world DB); trainer learn skills
# and prices from Forever's sniffed trainer lists; recipes and their skill colours
# from the Forever client tables (`forge data professions`).
# ASSUMED: past level 30 (the beta's cap) Forever's spawns are Classic's; nothing
# confirms them yet. In-game check: refine with Polestar_Recorder sessions.
# Rank level gates: Journeyman Fishing asks level 10 (Forever's sniffed trainer
# list); Cooking's and First Aid's Journeyman ask none (their sniffed lists, and
# players' recordings train them at 6 and 7). In-game check: reading an Expert
# book below level 20.
# Waypoints are Era-frame (`coords era`); the engine converts them where Forever
# changed a map frame, and a map without an Era frame (Zephras Isle) compiles live.
# ASSUMED: catches per point follow Classic's rate (every catch below 75, then
# one in (skill - 50) / 25) and a zone loses no fish from its Classic base skill
# + 95 (25 starting areas, 75 their neighbours, 150, 225 Stranglethorn, 300
# Feralas); Forever's notes say fishing is unchanged. In-game check: catches
# from 150 to 160, and fish lost at skill 1 in a starting area.
# ASSUMED: which fish bite in each band's water (Classic's fishing loot by zone
# level: lakes and rivers, the coast); the cooking recipes, their prices and
# their sellers are the data's.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice
section Fishing 1-50

step Learn Fishing
  tip Any Fishing trainer of your faction teaches Apprentice Fishing at any character level (1s); the arrow picks the nearest, and every starting area has one on its lake or shore. Buy a Fishing Pole (23c) from a trade goods or fishing vendor and equip it (you can only fish with a pole in your hands), and two or three Shiny Baubles (+25, 50c each): a lure adds its bonus to your skill for ten minutes, so fewer fish get away at the start. If you sat at your starting area's campfire for The Great Outdoors, the camping guide there also offers Camping 101: Fishing, handed in to the fishing trainer it names at skill 20 for the Fish Bowl recipe.
  train Fishing Apprentice
  buy 6256 x1 nearest

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Fishing 1-50

step Fishing: Elwynn Forest (1-50)
  only Human
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip Fish here until skill 50, about 50 catches: below 75 every catch raises the skill. Cast Fishing from your spellbook, click the bobber when it splashes. Keep the fish: they are your first Cooking ingredients. Fish get away here below skill 25; a lure on the pole adds to your skill for ten minutes and closes the gap. To cook what you catch: Recipe: Brilliant Smallfish for the Raw Brilliant Smallfish of lakes and rivers (Cooking 1, 40c: Tharynn Bouden (Elwynn Forest) or Catherine Leland (Stormwind City)); Recipe: Slitherskin Mackerel for the Raw Slitherskin Mackerel of the coast (Cooking 1, 40c: Kriggon Talsone (Westfall) or Tansy Puddlefizz (Ironforge)).
  goto 47.6,62.3 "Crystal Lake" r 25
  skill Fishing 50

